{"term":"recover","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:cc500b65b7d8b0a814","definition":"To get back, to regain (a physical thing; in astronomy and navigation, sight of a thing or a signal).","example":"After days of inquiries, he finally recovered his lost wallet.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["cryorecover","misrecover","overrecover","recoverability","recoverable","recoverance","recoveree","recoverin","recoveringly","recover one's senses","recoveror","unrecovered","recoverless"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recover#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:db84ff1a87aa81a4ca","definition":"To salvage, to extricate, to rescue (a thing or person).","example":"They recovered three of the explorers very much alive, then another, wracked with severe hypothermia, who was taken to hospital.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["cryorecover","misrecover","overrecover","recoverability","recoverable","recoverance","recoveree","recoverin","recoveringly","recover one's senses","recoveror","unrecovered","recoverless"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recover#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:672ab6aed0a56a51d1","definition":"To replenish to, resume (a good state of mind or body).","example":"At the top of the hill I asked to stop for a few minutes to recover my strength.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["cryorecover","misrecover","overrecover","recoverability","recoverable","recoverance","recoveree","recoverin","recoveringly","recover one's senses","recoveror","unrecovered","recoverless"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recover#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a6611953793ce043f3","definition":"To obtain a positive judgement; to win in a lawsuit.","example":"The plaintiff recovered in his suit, being awarded declaratory relief and a clearing of his name.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["cryorecover","misrecover","overrecover","recoverability","recoverable","recoverance","recoveree","recoverin","recoveringly","recover one's senses","recoveror","unrecovered","recoverless"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recover#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d7833f96c97de36cb8","definition":"To gain as compensation or reparation, usually by formal legal process.","example":"to recover damages in trespass; to recover debt and costs in a legal action or that is owing","pos":"verb","synonyms":["recoup"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["cryorecover","misrecover","overrecover","recoverability","recoverable","recoverance","recoveree","recoverin","recoveringly","recover one's senses","recoveror","unrecovered","recoverless"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recover#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4d2d15e04a5dd4c06b","definition":"To reach (a place), arrive at.","example":"The forest is not three leagues off; / If we recover that, we're sure enough.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["cryorecover","misrecover","overrecover","recoverability","recoverable","recoverance","recoveree","recoverin","recoveringly","recover one's senses","recoveror","unrecovered